## Getting started

Requires Git, Bash and mise. `just setup` installs pinned tools and Git hooks;
`just check` runs the offline, secret-free lint and test gate. `just --list` lists
available recipes. `just fmt` formats; `just doctor` checks tool/config presence offline.
`just smoke` is opt-in for live systems and never runs in CI.

## Customization and template updates

Put project recipes in `project.just`: project overrides archetype overrides base.
Archetype tools extend `mise.toml` through `.config/mise/conf.d/`.
Keep `.copier-answers.base.yml` and any archetype answers separate. Commit local
changes, then update the base with:

```sh
copier update --answers-file .copier-answers.base.yml --vcs-ref v0.1.0
just check
```

`project.just`, `fnox.toml`, `README.md`, `.agents/project.md` and workspace policy
starters are preserved when present; review base-owned changes during updates.

## Secrets

`fnox.toml` is project-owned and imports `.config/fnox/provider.toml`. Store only
references such as `TOKEN = { provider = "vault", value = "{{ project_slug }}/TOKEN" }`.
Bitwarden folder: {{ secrets_folder }}; item: {{ project_slug }}; fields: variable names.
Backend: `{{ bw_backend }}`{% if bw_profile %}, profile: `{{ bw_profile }}`{% endif %}.
Unlock the vault separately, and wrap only live operations with `fnox exec --`.
Never run vault unlock, network provisioning or `just smoke` from `just check`.
`just doctor` never resolves vault entries. Run `fnox check` only as a separately
authorized live gate when vault access is intended.

## Agent guidance

Read `AGENTS.md` (also available through relative `CLAUDE.md`) and any archetype
notes. `.omp/permissions.json` follows portable omp policy; local grants belong in
ignored `.omp/permissions.local.json`. Sandbox configuration describes intent,
not enforcement. Never commit credentials or widen access implicitly.
